# Mobile-native UI gate (always-on)

Every **UI change** in `src/**` must preserve the native mobile shell: bottom sheets, thumb-first actions, and no floating dropdown panels on phone.

## When this applies

- New or changed pages, components, modals, menus, toolbars, forms, cards, tables
- Layout, spacing, typography, or navigation on any screen
- **Skip:** backend/SQL with no UI; internal renames with no layout change

## Before implementing (mandatory)

1. Invoke **`mobile-responsive`** skill (`.agent/skills/mobile-responsive/SKILL.md`) on UI tasks.
2. Design mobile first at 375px; shell breakpoint is **`lg` (1024px)** / `max-width: 1023px`.
3. Reuse shared primitives in `src/lib/components/common/` and `src/lib/components/layout/`.

| Need | Use |
| ---- | --- |
| Modal / form | `ResponsiveModal` |
| Overflow ⋯ menu | `ResponsiveOverflowMenu` (+ `ActionMenuList` / `ActionSheetList`) |
| Bottom nav | `MobileTabBar` + `MobileMoreSheet` |
| List → detail on phone | `isMobileShellViewport()` → navigate to detail route |

## Hard rules below `lg`

- **No floating `DropdownMenu` panels** for overflow actions or option lists. Use `ResponsiveOverflowMenu` (sheet on phone, dropdown on desktop).
- **No centered `Dialog`** for forms or pickers. Use `ResponsiveModal` (sheet under `lg`).
- **Touch targets** ≥ 44×44px (`touch-target`, `min-h-11` on sheet rows).
- **One bottom nav layer.** Tab bar only; no second dock on detail pages.

## Desktop-only exception

`DropdownMenu` is allowed only where the trigger is **`hidden` below `lg`** (e.g. sidebar user menu in `Nav.svelte`). Never render a dropdown on viewports under `lg`.

## Before claiming UI work done

- [ ] 375px: overflow menus open as bottom sheets, not dropdowns
- [ ] Modals open as sheets on phone (`ResponsiveModal`)
- [ ] Route guide updated if page UX changed (`route-guides` skill)

Inventory: `docs/workflow/planned/mobile-native-redesign.md`.
